(1864714, 257109, 16648, '<td valign="top">I know this meets the challenge, but I am not a big fan on just cutting up one nice shot into 3 with distracting borders. Seems to easy, no real creativity required. I do not like the color of your border, but I do like your choise of a non-white non-black border. perhaps the green form the plants or the planters tan color would have been a bit better.</td>', 'I know this meets the challenge, but I am not a big fan on just cutting up one nice shot into 3 with distracting borders. Seems to easy, no real creativity required. I do not like the color of your border, but I do like your choise of a non-white non-black border. perhaps the green form the plants or the planters tan color would have been a bit better.', '2005-11-14 10:51:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1864718, 257343, 16648, '<td valign="top">PM me please - i need to know where you got those bulbs, or how you made this ''look'' like they are in the pic with the animals - i am doing pet portraits and have beenlooking for something to fill the lower front of the frame and this looks great.<br/> <br/>Photo wise, i mgiht have put the left panel in the center, dog-color wise, but then i suppsoe you chose based on bulb count? It''s always easy to second guess, huh?</td>', 'PM me please - i need to know where you got those bulbs, or how you made this ''look'' like they are in the pic with the animals - i am doing pet portraits and have beenlooking for something to fill the lower front of the frame and this looks great. Photo wise, i mgiht have put the left panel in the center, dog-color wise, but then i suppsoe you chose based on bulb count? It''s always easy to second guess, huh?', '2005-11-14 10:54:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1864720, 255392, 16648, '<td valign="top">I know this meets the challenge, but I am not a big fan on just cutting up one nice shot into 3 with distracting borders. Seems to easy, no real creativity required.  This is the first one i''ve seen with no outside border. makes me feel the divisions are just part of the window you are looking out - reduces the illusion of a tryptich.</td>', 'I know this meets the challenge, but I am not a big fan on just cutting up one nice shot into 3 with distracting borders. Seems to easy, no real creativity required.  This is the first one i''ve seen with no outside border. makes me feel the divisions are just part of the window you are looking out - reduces the illusion of a tryptich.', '2005-11-14 10:56:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1864723, 256814, 16648, '<td valign="top">I know this meets the challenge, but I am not a big fan on just cutting up one nice shot into 3 with distracting borders. Seems to easy, no real creativity required. A very nice shot otherwise, well composed.</td>', 'I know this meets the challenge, but I am not a big fan on just cutting up one nice shot into 3 with distracting borders. Seems to easy, no real creativity required. A very nice shot otherwise, well composed.', '2005-11-14 10:56:46.000000', NULL, 1),
