(1873053, 257395, 26255, '<td valign="top">The focus seems a little off and the highlights are a bit blown out.  Honestly I don''t think this image lends itself very well to a triptych.  There is no natural separation where you have chosen to break the image and the gray/brown background doesn''t help either.</td>', 'The focus seems a little off and the highlights are a bit blown out.  Honestly I don''t think this image lends itself very well to a triptych.  There is no natural separation where you have chosen to break the image and the gray/brown background doesn''t help either.', '2005-11-16 12:43:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1873065, 255852, 26255, '<td valign="top">Very interesting take on the challenge.  At first glance it doesn''t look like a triptych, then it does, but then is it a multiple exposure?  It can''t be a long exposure, it''s natural light.  The more I look at it the more I wonder how the heck you did that.  Honestly I can''t tell if it meets the challenge or not.  I''m giving it a 9 just for confusing the heck out of me</td>', 'Very interesting take on the challenge.  At first glance it doesn''t look like a triptych, then it does, but then is it a multiple exposure?  It can''t be a long exposure, it''s natural light.  The more I look at it the more I wonder how the heck you did that.  Honestly I can''t tell if it meets the challenge or not.  I''m giving it a 9 just for confusing the heck out of me', '2005-11-16 12:45:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1873070, 256898, 26255, '<td valign="top">Geesh... I''m a sucker for babies... No fair!  Nice compositions and arrangement.  I think I might prefer it as a horizontal triptych with a slightly narrower border, but that''s just a matter of taste.  Good image</td>', 'Geesh... I''m a sucker for babies... No fair!  Nice compositions and arrangement.  I think I might prefer it as a horizontal triptych with a slightly narrower border, but that''s just a matter of taste.  Good image', '2005-11-16 12:46:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1873100, 257394, 40718, '<td valign="top">whew, when you try to reshoot a shot already done (EddyG) and a difficult one at that, it''s hard not to compare.  I think you know already this did not match (no pun) up.  On it''s own merit, the smoke is fairly well captured.  The blue going off to the left is the weakest, the red is the strongest.</td>', 'whew, when you try to reshoot a shot already done (EddyG) and a difficult one at that, it''s hard not to compare.  I think you know already this did not match (no pun) up.  On it''s own merit, the smoke is fairly well captured.  The blue going off to the left is the weakest, the red is the strongest.', '2005-11-16 12:52:06.000000', NULL, 1),
