(1886478, 256840, 30861, '<td valign="top">I''m REALLY surprised this moody, beautiful image finished so far down. I expected a better placing from it.</td>', 'I''m REALLY surprised this moody, beautiful image finished so far down. I expected a better placing from it.', '2005-11-21 02:35:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(1886479, 257300, 17507, '<td valign="top">Hm, I should amend my comment from a few hours ago. It looked at first to me like the panels on the left and right were different sizes, but upon review in Photoshop they are exactly the same size. I dunno what was throwing me off visually. That''s cool that you did this all with one photograph. I hadn''t realized that. Looking at it now, I see that panel 1 is a reversed piece of panel 2. Interesting work. I think this might have been more effective with all three panels being the same size.</td>', 'Hm, I should amend my comment from a few hours ago. It looked at first to me like the panels on the left and right were different sizes, but upon review in Photoshop they are exactly the same size. I dunno what was throwing me off visually. That''s cool that you did this all with one photograph. I hadn''t realized that. Looking at it now, I see that panel 1 is a reversed piece of panel 2. Interesting work. I think this might have been more effective with all three panels being the same size.', '2005-11-21 02:36:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(1886480, 257310, 30861, '<td valign="top">You was robbed!</td>', 'You was robbed!', '2005-11-21 02:37:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(1886484, 257285, 30861, '<td valign="top">Yup! You''re in San Diego! Say hi to the cliffs for me, willya? I''m surprised this scored so low, except I guess the PP artifacts were just too much for the voters.</td>', 'Yup! You''re in San Diego! Say hi to the cliffs for me, willya? I''m surprised this scored so low, except I guess the PP artifacts were just too much for the voters.', '2005-11-21 02:40:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1886487, 256690, 3214, '<td valign="top">I wouldn''t consider 5.57 a failure...there are folks here that would''ve loved that score!   :-)</td>', 'I wouldn''t consider 5.57 a failure...there are folks here that would''ve loved that score!   :-)', '2005-11-21 02:44:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(1886490, 257191, 17507, '<td valign="top">Funny, I recently saw a squirrel performing some crazy acrobatics in an apparently desperate search for food. This guy was climbing through the upper branches of a persimmon tree, when in order to reach something on a nearby branch, he suspended himself from his little toes, completely upside down, and stretched downward still further. Seeing a squirrel hanging upside down was really weird, and he hung there for kind of a while. Agile little fellow that he was, he finished his business and continued clambering around without a single misstep. <br/> <br/>Anyway. I think the major thing this triptych could have used was a closer crop on the squirrel/bird feeder... something that takes us close to the action and really lets us see what''s going on. I liked this picture, though - it made me smile.<br/> <br/>edited for grammar ~_~<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-11-21 02:46:09.</i></td>', 'Funny, I recently saw a squirrel performing some crazy acrobatics in an apparently desperate search for food. This guy was climbing through the upper branches of a persimmon tree, when in order to reach something on a nearby branch, he suspended himself from his little toes, completely upside down, and stretched downward still further. Seeing a squirrel hanging upside down was really weird, and he hung there for kind of a while. Agile little fellow that he was, he finished his business and continued clambering around without a single misstep.  Anyway. I think the major thing this triptych could have used was a closer crop on the squirrel/bird feeder... something that takes us close to the action and really lets us see what''s going on. I liked this picture, though - it made me smile. edited for grammar ~_~', '2005-11-21 02:45:29.000000', '2005-11-21 02:46:09.000000', 0),
