(1975232, 257197, 49865, '<td valign="top">I love how the colors are arranged in this. Reminds me of an almost rock-papper-scissors succession. The green of the first leaf becomes the background for the second panel. The yellow of that the background for the third, and the red of the third the background for the first. Pulls me right into the picture, directing my eyes left to right and back to the beginning again. That having been said, I think the thickness of the borders is a bit of an obstruction - something slightly thinner and maybe lighter might make this more powerful. Someone suggested a dark brown.<br/> <br/>One of my favorites.</td>', 'I love how the colors are arranged in this. Reminds me of an almost rock-papper-scissors succession. The green of the first leaf becomes the background for the second panel. The yellow of that the background for the third, and the red of the third the background for the first. Pulls me right into the picture, directing my eyes left to right and back to the beginning again. That having been said, I think the thickness of the borders is a bit of an obstruction - something slightly thinner and maybe lighter might make this more powerful. Someone suggested a dark brown. One of my favorites.', '2005-12-24 07:09:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(1978719, 257077, 37719, '<td valign="top">This is an excellent photo with quite a feel to it.  The plant just seems to be reaching right through the frames/screen.  Great clarity, excellent DoF, good colors!  Well done!</td>', 'This is an excellent photo with quite a feel to it.  The plant just seems to be reaching right through the frames/screen.  Great clarity, excellent DoF, good colors!  Well done!', '2005-12-26 11:23:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(1987058, 257307, 38706, '<td valign="top">I put this in a recent <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=114444" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">conversation</a> and figured it really belongs as a comment on the photo directly.  Great shot....<br/> <br/>I find it hard to come up with a composition with a few people in it that is more than the usual blah blah stuff. This one keeps the connection between the 3 people in each frame while clearly highlighting the individual. While each shot is good as a seperate thing the set of 3 just work well together and I loved the idea. It really does convey the friends theme between the 3 girls.</td>', 'I put this in a recent conversation and figured it really belongs as a comment on the photo directly.  Great shot.... I find it hard to come up with a composition with a few people in it that is more than the usual blah blah stuff. This one keeps the connection between the 3 people in each frame while clearly highlighting the individual. While each shot is good as a seperate thing the set of 3 just work well together and I loved the idea. It really does convey the friends theme between the 3 girls.', '2005-12-29 20:04:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(1992649, 256893, 34659, '<td valign="top">Scored this a 7 during the challenge.  I love llamas (we used to raise them when I was growing up), but boy are they tempermental!  Great series of expressions and poses.  The lighting is a tad harsh, but I''m grasping at straws...  Terrific job.</td>', 'Scored this a 7 during the challenge.  I love llamas (we used to raise them when I was growing up), but boy are they tempermental!  Great series of expressions and poses.  The lighting is a tad harsh, but I''m grasping at straws...  Terrific job.', '2006-01-01 15:45:58.000000', NULL, 0),
